              + $150 permit + labor 10 h × $95 = $950<br />
              total = <span class="font-bold text-emerald-700">$4,620</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
              <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Result:</span> the upgrade is 66% of the job. This is
              exactly the case to test against NEC 220.87 first — and to price a 32 A charger as the alternative.
            </p>
          </div>
